cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use UV-Vis Spectrum Studio in research, cite the exact software release used. After Zenodo archives a release, prefer the DOI assigned to that archived version."
title: "UV-Vis Spectrum Studio"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hasan
    given-names: Abdulsalam S.
    affiliation: "University of Mosul, College of Science, Department of Chemistry"
version: 3.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-17
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/abd19990044-commits/uv-vis-spectrum-studio"
url: "https://github.com/abd19990044-commits/uv-vis-spectrum-studio"
abstract: >-
  UV-Vis Spectrum Studio is open-source, cross-platform scientific software for
  UV-Vis spectroscopy and analytical chemistry. It provides spectral import and
  cleaning, publication-quality visualization, derivative spectroscopy through
  fourth order with quality safeguards, quantitative calibration and analytical-
  method validation, multicomponent spectrophotometry, peak fitting and
  deconvolution, Fourier/wavelet analysis, chemometrics with fold-safe supervised
  preprocessing and nested PLS validation, and reproducible tamper-evident
  project archives.
keywords:
  - UV-Vis spectroscopy
  - analytical chemistry
  - spectrophotometry
  - chemometrics
  - analytical method validation
  - derivative spectrophotometry
  - peak deconvolution
  - multicomponent analysis
  - spectral processing
  - reproducible research
  - scientific software
